      "problem": "Express $\\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}$ as a base raised to a single number.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the numerator using the product rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}= \\dfrac{5^{4+2}}{5^3} = \\dfrac{5^{6}}{5^3}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5^6}{5^3} = 5^{6-3} = 5^{3}\n$$",
